Unit 4: UI Components
=====================
4.1 System menus and functions of menus
4.2 Formatting of menus: Consistency, display, presentation, organization, complexity
    , item arrangement, ordering, grouping
4.3 Types of menus: Menu bar, pull down menu, cascading menu, popup menu, tear off
    menu, iconic menu
4.4 Selection of windows and its  components, window presentation styles: Tiled win-
    dows, overlapping windows, cascading windows
4.5 Types of windows: Primary windows, secondary windows, dialog boxes
4.6 Screen based controls: Operable controls: (Buttons, toolbars), Text entry/Read
    -only controls (Single and multiple line textboxes), selection controls (radio 
     buttons, checkboxes, palettes, list boxes, list view controls, drop down/popup
     list boxes
4.7  Other operable controls: slider, tabs, date picker, tree view, scroll bars
4.8  Selecting the proper controls
4.9  Creating meaningful graphics, icons and images 

